   "text": "CSS Grouping Selectors"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The CSS Universal Selector"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The universal selector (*) selects all HTML elements on the page."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "css",
   "text": "*\n{\n\n  text-align: center;\n\n  color: blue;\n\n}",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=trycss_syntax_universal"
  },
  {
   "type": "h2",
   "text": "The CSS Grouping Selector"
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "The grouping selector selects all the HTML elements with the same style\ndefinitions."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Look at the following CSS code (the h1, h2, and p elements have the same\nstyle definitions):"
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "css",
   "text": "h1\n{\n\n  text-align: center;\n  color: red;\n\n}\n\nh2\n{\n\ntext-align: center;\n  color: red;\n}\n\np\n{\n\n  text-align: center;\n  color: red;\n\n}",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "It will be better to group the selectors, to minimize the code."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "To group selectors, separate each selector with a comma."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "lang": "css",
   "text": "h1, h2, p\n{\n\ntext-align: center;\n  color: red;\n}",
   "caption": "Example"
  },
  {
   "type": "tryit",
   "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=trycss_grouping"
  },
  {
